        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(docker): bound smoke installer curl with connect timeout",
        "body": "AI-assisted: yes. I reviewed and understand the change.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe install-sh-smoke Docker runner executes a direct `curl | bash` one-liner (line 337) with no overall pipeline timeout. While `run_installer_for_package_spec` and the freshness path use `timeout(1)` to bound the complete pipeline, this direct invocation had only curl-level timeout flags — the post-download bash execution could still hang indefinitely.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nWrap the entire `curl | bash` pipeline in `timeout --kill-after=30s \"${INSTALL_COMMAND_TIMEOUT}s\"`, matching the existing `run_installer_for_package_spec` pattern. The curl-level `--connect-timeout 30` and `--max-time 300` flags are retained as defence-in-depth inside the timeout wrapper — the process-level timeout bounds the complete pipeline (download + install), while the curl-level timeouts fail fast on network stalls without waiting for the full command timeout.\n\n## User Impact\n\nSmoke test CI jobs now fail within the configured `INSTALL_COMMAND_TIMEOUT` (default 900 s) when either the download or the subsequent installation hangs. This matches the existing behavior of `run_installer_for_package_spec` and the freshness smoke path.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs test/scripts/test-install-sh-docker.test.ts --run -t \"runs candidate tarballs\"`: passed.\n- The guard test verifies both the `timeout --kill-after=30s` wrapper and the `--connect-timeout 30 --max-time 300` flags.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n\n### Real behavior proof\n\nHealthy path — a normal HTTPS transfer completes well within the timeout:\n\n```\n$ curl -fsSL --connect-timeout 30 --max-time 300 -o /dev/null   -w 'HTTP %{http_code}, time_total: %{time_total}s' https://openclaw.bot/install.sh\nHTTP 200, time_total: 0.8s\n```\n\nStalled path — connecting to a non-routable address exits within the connect-timeout bound:\n\n```\n$ curl -fsSL --connect-timeout 3 --max-time 10 -o /dev/null 'https://10.255.255.1:9999/'\ncurl: (28) Connection timed out after 3013 milliseconds\n```\n\nThe outer `timeout --kill-after=30s \"${INSTALL_COMMAND_TIMEOUT}s\"` bounds the complete `curl|bash` pipeline, while the inner `--connect-timeout 30 --max-time 300` provides early network-stall detection without waiting for the full command timeout.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
